{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"grim-flavoured-bull","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`rebar store fsck` parses its argv by hand (`fsck_cli`, `src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py`). It picks out the flags it knows (`--repair`, `--dry-run`, `--repair-snapshots`, `--include-archived`, `--only`, `--limit`, the output flags) and drops everything else, so an unknown or misspelled flag exits 0 with no message.\n\nObserved on origin/main `aa1681bb531` in a scratch store (2026-11-13):\n- `rebar store fsck --bogus` exits 0 and runs a normal check.\n- `rebar store fsck --limit` (no value) exits 0; the bare flag is dropped.\n- `rebar store fsck --repair --dryrun` (typo for `--dry-run`) runs the REAL repair: output `ensures: swept 10 unit(s); 0 changed, 0 failed`, where `--repair --dry-run` only reports. A typo turns a preview into a mutation of the store.\n\n`rebar store compact` already rejects unknown options (`Error: unknown option '--threshold'`, exit 1), so fsck is the odd one out.\n\n## Approach\nIn `fsck_cli`, after the known flags are taken out and `parse_output` runs, reject any leftover argument: write `Error: unknown option '<arg>'` plus the usage line to stderr and return 2, before any store access or repair. Reject a bare `--limit` the same way `--only` already is (`Error: --limit requires a value`, exit 2). No new flag, config key or env var.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar store fsck --bogus` exits 2 and stderr names `--bogus`.\n- [ ] `rebar store fsck --repair --dryrun` exits 2 and makes no change to the store (no ensure sweep, no commit).\n- [ ] `rebar store fsck --limit` exits 2 with `--limit requires a value`.\n- [ ] Every documented spelling still works: `--only stale-channel --repair`, `--only=stale-channel --repair`, `--limit 1`, `--limit=1`, `--include-archived`, `--repair-snapshots`, `--dry-run`, and the output flags; proved by `pytest tests/unit/test_fsck_only_flag.py`.\n\n## Testing\nAdd RED tests to `tests/unit/test_fsck_only_flag.py` for the 3 rejected forms (exit 2, message, and for the typo case no repair call), then make them pass. Run `pytest tests/unit/test_fsck_only_flag.py` and `make verify`.","id":"d631-a767-1327-48f1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar store fsck silently ignores unknown flags, so a typo'd --dry-run runs a real repair"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794590359114571973,"uuid":"32e92fb0-fc90-4262-ad92-5ae5786c821a"}